// =====================================================================
// Classic network headers: a showcase for bit-sized fields, split over
// files with `import`.
//
// - net/ethernet.packet: Ethernet II frames; it imports net/ip.packet.
// - net/ip.packet: IPv4, TCP and UDP headers, with option lists.
// - net/dns.packet: DNS messages with name compression.
//
// Decoding an Ethernet frame decodes everything inside it: the EtherType
// and the IP protocol pick the next header (tagged unions, `switch`).
// =====================================================================

import "net/ethernet.packet"
import "net/ip.packet"   // already imported by ethernet.packet: loaded once
import "net/dns.packet"
